 A lexical-only local index is insufficient and provably so.'","c670 Approach: 'The credentials-absent skip is widened to catch AccessDeniedException, recording candidate 3 unavailable with the error instead of aborting — and an unavailable candidate may not be selected by the ADR.'","c670 AC2: 'Recall@5 and recall@10 are recorded per stratum for all three candidates' — but candidate 3 can be recorded 'unavailable' rather than measured.","iam_s7.tf:16-17 confirms only anthropic.claude-* ARNs are entitled; no Titan/embedding ARN exists.","container pairing: parent + c670-c285-a0f9-4b40"],"finding":"c670 admits the vector candidate (candidate 3, Titan amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0) may come back 'unavailable' (AccessDeniedException, no production entitlement) and states 'an unavailable candidate may not be selected by the ADR' — which conflicts with the parent epic's premise that the architecture is justified from the semantic stratum and the operator framing 'This is a vector search problem over summaries.' If candidate 3 is skipped, c670 can still produce a passing ADR (lexical + digest strata measured) that selects a non-vector architecture, structurally contradicting the epic's reopened-embedding decision and leaving parent AC1's semantic-stratum justification resting on a candidate that was never run.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f79ffcca248544481","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"child c670-c285-a0f9-4b40","norm_id":"nbb4f037aebfe2117","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Developer AWS identity with Titan entitlement is not obtained and the Titan ARN is not added to iam_s7.tf; c670 records candidate 3 'unavailable', the ADR selects the digest-lexical architecture, and the epic's vector-search premise is silently abandoned while AC1's checker (per-stratum tables present) still passes."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add to c670: if candidate 3 is recorded 'unavailable', the ADR is not completable an